## 2026-05-22T02:10:12Z - commit 11 / kernel program add handles roots and seeds

- Summary: Implemented `mfm-program` branded program handles, checked root/seed/public-output keys, canonical root seed specs, deterministic root scope and seed cell ids, `build_root`, `RootBuilder`, `ScopeBuilder`, private typed handle references, non-forgeable public output cell/spec construction from real handles, and typed program draft accessors. Extended `mfm-program-derive` so `#[derive(PublicOutputs)]` on handle-bearing program output structs generates `mfm_program::PublicOutputs<'program, 'scope>` evidence and binds public output cells from handles. Added unit tests plus trybuild pass/fail fixtures for root construction, forged handles/specs, escaped handles, missing public-output binding, swapped output lifetimes, stale root evidence, and runtime values used as seeds. Extended the manual persisted-trait source-boundary checker self-test to cover `mfm_program::PublicOutputs` manual impls. Stabilized unrelated test gates that surfaced during full-suite validation: the exec stdout overflow timeout now reports the intended overflow error reliably under load, and the keystore MAC tamper test now always changes the selected MAC byte.
- Tests run and results: `cargo test -p mfm-program` passed; `cargo test -p mfm-program-derive` passed; `cargo test -p mfm-program program_authoring_accepts_and_rejects_branded_handles` passed under both the host Rust 1.91 toolchain and the Nix Rust 1.92 toolchain; `cargo nextest run --cargo-profile ci -p mfm-program -p mfm-program-derive --fail-fast` passed under the Nix toolchain; `cargo nextest run --cargo-profile ci --workspace --fail-fast` initially passed with 799/799 tests before the stale-root fix, then exposed an unrelated randomized keystore MAC tamper no-op after the stale-root fix; `cargo nextest run --cargo-profile ci -p mfm_core test_tampered_audit_log_and_mac_fail_integrity --fail-fast` passed after making the tamper deterministic; a full direct `cargo nextest run --cargo-profile ci --workspace --fail-fast` rerun passed with 799/799 tests, and the suspected leaky CLI parse-error test also passed in isolation; `cargo nextest run --cargo-profile ci -p mfm-transports-exec stdout_overflow_reports_bounded_failure_metadata --fail-fast` passed; `cargo fmt -p mfm-program -p mfm-program-derive -p mfm-transports-exec -- --check` passed; `cargo clippy -p mfm-program -p mfm-program-derive --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed; `nixfied/project/check-manual-persisted-impls.sh --root . --self-test --summary-file /tmp/mfm-manual-program-output-summary.json` passed; `git diff --check` passed; `nix run .#test` passed after the deterministic keystore test fix and final wrapper rerun.
- Design decisions: Handles are invariant in both program and scope lifetimes and in `T`, with private constructors and private typed-ref fields so callers can carry handles but cannot forge handle/spec identity. `RootBound` is also invariant in program and scope lifetimes and is not `Clone`, so stale root evidence from one program build cannot certify a different root. Handles are `Clone` rather than `Copy` because current typed ids own validated strings. Public output specs are built through derive-generated handle-bearing structs instead of caller-supplied cell ids; this keeps the public binding tied to program-authored handles. The program-level public-output trait remains public only as a derive target, with manual impls rejected by the source-boundary checker until certification can rely on generated evidence. Canonical seeds validate that seed bytes decode as `T`; deterministic ids currently use digest-derived typed ids rather than embedding runtime values in seeds.
